# Major Feature Delivery

When a major project section is complete and verified, default to the complete delivery workflow without asking which Git option to use:

1. Update the feature branch from the current `main` branch.
2. Run the relevant full verification suite and fix failures.
3. Push the feature branch and create or update its pull request.
4. Get required CI checks green and merge the pull request into `main`.
5. Update the local `main` checkout.
6. Deploy each affected live component using the repository runbook.
7. Refresh or republish live read models when the release changes their schema or contents.
8. Verify the deployed version and report the PR and deployment result.

Preserve unrelated user changes. Never force-push, bypass failing checks, expose secrets, or perform destructive cleanup without explicit authorization.
